.TH FASTRDP-BROKERD 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdp-brokerd \- session broker of the fastrdp RDP terminal server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdp-brokerd
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fastrdp-brokerd
authenticates users for the fastrdp proxy module (password, account and MFA
checks), chooses each user's desktop back end (xrdp, GNOME Remote Desktop,
Plasma/KRdp), starts the back-end session and issues the one-time tokens that
the back ends accept.
It normally runs as
.BR fastrdp-brokerd.service ,
which is installed disabled: write
.I /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml
first (see the example in
.IR /usr/share/doc/fastrdp-broker/examples/ ),
then run
.BR "systemctl enable \-\-now fastrdp-brokerd" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " config\fR, " \-\-config " config"
Configuration file (default
.IR /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the configuration and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml
Configuration (mode 0600, root).
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/fastrdp
PAM service for password and account checks.
.TP
.I /run/fastrdp
Sockets, desktop choices and session environment files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdpctl (8)
